GNOME Keyring 51.1 OpenSession hotfix
==================================

The source branch backports the two original commits from GNOME merge request
!112 onto release 51.1, plus a local disconnected-client cleanup follow-up.
The original patch is proposed upstream, not merged or approved. It repairs the
missing-client registration race and prevents failed negotiation from becoming a
NULL success reply that aborts the daemon. The follow-up watches initial name
ownership as well as future disconnects, releasing state if a queued request
recreates a client after its disconnect notification was already processed.
Queued registration also stops once service disposal clears the connection.

Upstream patch:
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-keyring/-/merge_requests/112
Matching client report:
https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/51694

This local PKGBUILD replaces ONLY /usr/bin/gnome-keyring-daemon. All other
payload files, service units, D-Bus activation files, PAM modules and package
install hooks come unchanged from the SHA-256-pinned Arch 1:51.1-1 package.
It generates fresh package metadata and mtree using makepkg. The replacement
daemon includes its debug symbols for subsequent diagnosis.

Build and validate
------------------

Use Meson, Ninja, GLib development tools and the normal Arch build dependencies.
No credentials, collection data or settings belong in this checkout.

  (
    source /etc/makepkg.conf
    export CFLAGS="$CFLAGS ${DEBUG_CFLAGS:--g}"
    export LDFLAGS
    meson setup .git/build-hardened --prefix=/usr --libdir=lib --libexecdir=lib \
      --sbindir=bin --buildtype=plain --wrap-mode=nodownload \
      -Dselinux=disabled -Dmanpage=false -Db_pie=true -Db_lto=true
    meson compile -C .git/build-hardened
  )

Building outside makepkg requires explicitly passing its compiler/linker flags.
The package recipe rejects a daemon missing PIE, BIND_NOW, stack protection or
fortified libc calls. Do not replace this build with an unhardened debug build.

Run the full Meson suite on a private D-Bus and a throwaway HOME/XDG environment;
the suite's daemon fixtures use temporary keyrings. Do not suppress test failures.
See validation/README.md for the standalone OpenSession concurrency regression,
which creates its own private bus with activation disabled.

After the build and validation pass, stage the installation into the checkout:

  meson install -C .git/build-hardened --destdir "$PWD/.git/stage"
  cd packaging
  makepkg --force

The original package is read from /var/cache/pacman/pkg by default. Override
GNOME_KEYRING_STOCK_PACKAGE to point at another copy of that EXACT archive.
Verify its detached Arch signature before building. The pinned checksum rejects
any other archive. Keep the original package and signature for rollback.

Installation and rollback
-------------------------

Install the generated gnome-keyring-1:51.1-1.2-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst with pacman -U.
This covers systemd, D-Bus and PAM because the existing /usr/bin path is retained.
Installing the package does not itself restart the running user daemon. A normal
logout/login activates the new binary; an explicit service restart activates it
immediately but discards session-only secrets and may require reauthentication.
Persistent keyring files are not modified by the package.

Rollback: install the original signed 1:51.1-1 archive with pacman -U, then use
the same deliberate restart/logout policy. No configuration override needs to be
removed. A later official package with a higher pkgrel/version replaces this
local package normally; it can reintroduce the defect if it lacks the patch.
Do not pin or block future security updates.

The original merge request remains the upstream contribution. Any GitHub PR for
this branch is a personal review/backport record, not a second upstream fix.
